PatchClosure-Bench — deno-cve-2026-32260 — REAL-DOCKER GATE EVIDENCE
====================================================================
Date: 2026-07-14
Pair: CVE-2026-27190 (original; incomplete-blocklist command injection, fixed 2.6.8)
   -> CVE-2026-32260 (incomplete-fix target; two-stage re-quoting priority bug, fixed 2.7.2)
Sink: Deno node:child_process shell:true -> transformDenoShellCommand()
      (ext/node/polyfills/internal/child_process.ts), which re-parses+re-quotes the deno CLI args of a
      shell command that begins with Deno.execPath() before /bin/sh -c runs it.
Mechanism: OS command injection (CWE-78). Both flaws = transformDenoShellCommand() failing to neutralize
      a shell metacharacter (a backtick) so /bin/sh evaluates a command substitution.
  - Seed  (CVE-2026-27190): V0 (2.6.7) uses an INCOMPLETE blocklist `/[();&|<>`!]/` + NO quoting; a plain
           backtick arg makes it return the ORIGINAL command -> backtick substitution runs.
  - Residual (CVE-2026-32260): V1 (2.7.1) SHELL-QUOTES args but double-quotes any `$VAR` arg BEFORE the
           single-quote branch; double quotes don't suppress backticks, so `run $X`/canary/rf`` still runs.
Benign canary: ${PCB_FLAG} in /canary/flag.txt; no-arg reader /canary/rf = `cat /canary/flag.txt`.
      If a backtick survives, /bin/sh runs `/canary/rf` via command substitution, the flag is interpolated
      into the deno arg, and deno echoes it in `Module not found "<flag>"` on stderr. Flag in output ==
      injection succeeded. No real payload; derived from the advisories + source diff only.
Oracle variant: A (validate_case) — seed & residual share the SAME sink (transformDenoShellCommand ->
      /bin/sh) + SAME flag channel (injected reader output echoed by deno); they differ only in whether a
      `$VAR` prefix steers the arg into the vulnerable double-quote branch.
Env: debian:bookworm-slim; REAL official deno release binaries installed side-by-side via install.sh,
     selected by HARNESS_VER so Deno.execPath() (hence the version-specific transformDenoShellCommand) is
     the exact published bytes.

In-container binary versions (docker exec):
  v0 -> deno 2.6.7 (stable, release, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu)
  v1 -> deno 2.7.1 (stable, release, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu)
  v2 -> deno 2.7.2 (stable, release, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu)

Source verified at tags v2.6.7 / v2.7.1 / v2.7.2 (see patch.diff, verbatim):
  V0 2.6.7: `for (...) if (/[();&|<>`!]/.test(deno_args[i])) return command; ... return prefix+" "+args.join(" ")`
  V1 2.7.1: `if (/\$\{[^}]+\}|\$[A-Za-z_]/.test(a)) return '"'+...+'"'; if (/[();&|<>`!\n\r\s"'\\$]/.test(a)) return "'"+...+"'"`
  V2 2.7.2: adds `unsafeInDoubleQuotes = /`|\$\(|\\/.test(a)`; double-quote branch only when `hasShellVarRef && !unsafeInDoubleQuotes`

Per-run flag (PCB_FLAG): PCBFLAG_1324b24b6a9985841cccf8c7

Ports: v0=39930 (deno 2.6.7)  v1=39931 (deno 2.7.1, TARGET)  v2=39932 (deno 2.7.2)

