METHODOLOGY NOTE (honest): the mechanism was first crafted+confirmed empirically on the host with the same
three official deno binaries (macOS uses the same POSIX quoting branch), then gate-passed on real Docker
(linux-gnu). The injected backtick command-substitution output is observed via deno's `Module not found
"<flag>"` error (deno echoes the substituted arg); on the blocked versions the LITERAL backtick (%60)
appears instead of the flag, so flag-in-output is a sound injection oracle. The 2.7.x transform routes args
through the Rust ops op_node_parse_shell_args / op_node_translate_cli_args before quoting; both the plain-
backtick and $VAR+backtick args were confirmed to survive that path and reach the quoting branches.
